WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:10.950
17. The eye in the sky. How cool would it be to have a flying robot?

2
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:16.950
What's the first thing you would do with it? Maybe send it into battle or use it to spy on your neighbors?

3
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:25.950
Well, this is not just a fantasy anymore. Drones are remote-controlled flying robots and they are getting more popular every day.

4
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.950
But is this a good thing for society?

5
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:35.950
The popularity of drones has exploded in recent years as technology has improved and gotten cheaper.

6
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:43.950
A standard drone with a high-quality camera and four helicopter propellers now sells online for just a few hundred US dollars.

7
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:50.950
Drones are extremely useful for making videos because their cameras link directly to phones or tablets.

8
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:55.950
Nowadays, anyone can get professional-looking flyby shots from unique angles.

9
00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:04.950
But could this cause problems? Because drones are so affordable, it means that anyone can send a robot flying around the neighborhood.

10
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:08.950
People might be surprised to find a camera floating outside their window.

11
00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:13.950
This should be a huge concern for people who care about their privacy.

12
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:18.950
Many governments also invest in drones, but for very different reasons.

13
00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.950
The United States uses military drones for spying.

14
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:30.950
Its most powerful drones, however, are Predator drones, which can fly higher than 15,000 meters at over 300 kilometers per hour.

15
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.950
And no, they don't just take pretty videos.

16
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:41.950
A Predator drone can hold 360 kilograms worth of bombs, enough to completely destroy an enemy camp.

17
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:48.950
The soldier controlling the drone sits safely away from the action, so it's impossible to know for sure who is getting killed.

18
00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.950
Innocent people might be in danger.

19
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:56.950
Drones are very new technology and people are still exploring their possible uses.

20
00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:02.950
Maybe someday you'll come up with a new, cool way to use your own remote-controlled robot.
